  "notes": {
    "call_counter": "Logged turns (4,795) exceed manifest totals.calls (4,794) by exactly the one failed turn. In the collection harness (freeze commit 435d20d, harness.py ClaudeCode.__call__) totals.calls is incremented only for a successful logical call; a call that exhausts its three attempts goes to Backend._fail, which increments totals.errors instead. The replay requires logged_turns == manifest_calls + manifest_errors and failed_turns == manifest_errors. Transport retries inside a logical call, and their cost and served model, were not recorded by that harness (changed after the freeze in 57d13c3).",
    "committed_analysis": "The committed heldout-haiku.jsonl.analysis.md was produced by the analyzer at the freeze commit (analyze.py, scoring.py, harness.py at 435d20d; identical blobs at a757306, the commit that added the results). The replay regenerates it byte-identically from those hash-pinned sources (analysis_collection.md). The snapshot analyzer (e056c88) output (analysis_snapshot.md) differs only by two added paired-count columns in the contrast table and a longer contrast note; the replay asserts that removing those columns gives the committed table and that the committed note's sentences all appear in the new note.",
    "rebuild": "Each trial is re-executed through provenance.run_trial with a replay backend that returns the logged raw replies in order (and fails the logged failed turn). The rebuilt row must equal the stored row except per-turn ms (wall time), per-turn fail_reason (added to the turn log after collection), and run metadata added by provenance.main."
